<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; this.result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>

Explanation:
- The comment specifies that if `fromIndex` is greater than or equal to -1, then for every index `i` that is greater than the result and less than or equal to `fromIndex`, the bit at index `i` in the `BitSet` is `false`.
- We use `\result` to refer to the return value of the `previousSetBit` method.
- The condition `\forall int i; this.result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);` ensures that for all indices `i` that satisfy `this.result < i && i <= fromIndex`, the bit at index `i` is `false`.
--------------------
<code>assert fromIndex >= -1 => \forall int i; \result < i && i <= fromIndex; !this.get(i);</code>
